+// V3D (Raspberry Pi 4/5) runs ggml's graphs correctly but far slower than the host CPU it shares
+// memory with. Measured on a Pi 4 against its four A72s: a VITS synthesis 64.9 s against 0.836 s
+// (the same audio to 1e-5), Qwen3-0.6B Q8_0 24 tokens 509 s against 4.2 s (the same tokens). Its
+// peak (32 GFLOPS, no FMA) is a third of theirs, so no tuning closes that. Offered by default it would
+// be chosen over the CPU by anything that prefers a GPU, so it is opt-in: name it in
+// GGML_VK_VISIBLE_DEVICES (loom patch ggml-0055).
+static bool ggml_vk_device_is_slower_than_host(const vk::PhysicalDevice & dev) {
+    vk::PhysicalDeviceProperties2 props;
+    vk::PhysicalDeviceDriverProperties driver;
+    props.pNext = &driver;
+    dev.getProperties2(&props);
+    return driver.driverID == vk::DriverId::eMesaV3Dv;
+}
